ind)\n\nBut in the valid actions list: 0 is included, along with 694+.\n\nAh — likely, **0 here means call** the 347 raise.\n\nBecause if you don’t want to fold or raise, calling 347 is represented as 0? That doesn\'t align.\n\nWait — common convention in some systems: \n- If you need to call X, then:\n  - -1 = fold\n  - 0 = call\n  - >0 = raise by that amount or to that amount?\n\nBut the description says: ">0 for the amount you raise the bet"\n\nSo if you raise by 694, you’re adding 694 **to the current required bet**? Or making total bet 694?\n\nAmbiguous.\n\nBut given: “raise the bet” → likely means **the amount you add above the current call amount**.\n\nAnd “must be at least twice the current maximum bet of this round” — unclear.\n\nBetter interpretation from context: the **minimum raise** is **694**, meaning you must bet at least **694 chips more than the current bet to call**.\n\nSo to call: 347\nTo raise: at least 347 + 694 = **1,041 total additional**\n\nBut your chip stack is 19,650 — plenty.\n\nValid actions: [-2, -1, 0, 694, or any value above 694 up to 19,650]\n\nSo:\n- -1: Fold\n- 0: Likely **Call** the 347\n- 694+: Raise by that amount (i.e., add 694 or more to the current bet)\n\nTherefore:\n- Calling costs 347 → total contribution on turn: 100 + 347 = 447\n- Raising by 694 means you bet 347 (call) + 694 (raise) = **1,041 additional**\n\nNow, evaluating:\n\nOption 1: Fold (-1)  \n→ Throwing away a full house. Extremely weak play unless certain beaten. But you have Kings full — only losing to flush or quads. Unlikely.\n\nOption 2: Call (0)  \n→ See the river cheaply. Good if you think you\'re ahead, but miss value.\n\nOption 3: Raise by 694 or more  \n→ You have a very strong hand. If opponent has a flush (e.g., A♦x♦), they might call. If bluffing, may fold. This extracts value.\n\nBut opponent raised you on the turn — they likely have:\n- Diamond flush (strong possibility)\n- Or slow-playing 10s or 6s\n- Or semi-bluffing with straight draws?\n\nBut 