o pair), but could also get called by better hands (like A-Q). Given pot size and previous bets, the pot is likely large already, so small additional bets may not be worth the risk.\n\nGoing all-in (-2) is unnecessary overkill and likely folds everyone worse while calling with better.\n\nChecking maintains your aggression history and lets you see showdown without risking more chips.\n\nReason:  \nYou have a decent two-pair hand, but the board texture favors draws that may have missed. Your opponent showed weakness by checking back on the river. Since you've already extracted value in earlier rounds and the effective stacks are deep, **checking to showdown is safest**. It avoids bluffing into a stronger hand and doesn’t risk losing more chips unnecessarily. You’re ahead in the match and should avoid high-risk plays unless necessary.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
