likely. However, your opponent has shown passivity, so aggressive action *could* work as a bluff — but without clear evidence of fold tendency, and considering your chip lead and position, it's better to minimize risk. Checking preserves chips and maintains pressure in future hands.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
