old (-1)**: Premature. You still have outs: possible flush (if another Club comes), or even pairing your Queen for two pair (Aces and Queens). Board isn’t heavily coordinated, so folding to no aggression is too tight.\n\nReason:  \nChecking is optimal. You have **top pair (Aces)** with a **decent kicker (Queen)** and **backdoor flush draw potential** (needing one more Club on River). Since the opponent checked first on the Turn, they may be weak or slow-playing. By checking back, you **see the River card for free**, preserving chips while retaining equity. You maintain initiative and avoid overcommitting with a medium-strength hand.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
